{"timestamp":"2026-08-01T07:06:36.507Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_08e2f0ae12d4839f016a6d9afb0d288190a922c1830443852b","status":"completed","call_id":"call_KlakNHYeoB94dmJ8dIwu2oNs","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"sed -n '1,260p' /codex-home/skills/using-kit/SKILL.md && rg -n \\\"proof-extension|PROOF.md|Gate A|Incomplete work\\\" /codex-home/skills -g 'SKILL.md' -g '*.md'\",\"workdir\":\"/workspace\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":20000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019fbc0a-4fc6-72c2-9e5b-aa0fa99c52de"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-01T07:06:36.584Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","call_id":"call_KlakNHYeoB94dmJ8dIwu2oNs","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---\nname: using-kit\ndescription: 'Use when starting any K-framework program-verification task — proving partial correctness, formalizing a language in K, writing K specs or proofs — or whenever unsure which kit skill applies.'\n---\n\n## What this kit proves\n\nThis kit proves **partial correctness**: if a program terminates and its\nprecondition holds, then its postcondition holds at termination.\n\n`kprove` establishes reachability claims by symbolic execution. For a loop, an\ninvariant claim acts coinductively as a **circularity**: when execution returns\nto a matching symbolic loop-head configuration, the prover may apply that claim\ninstead of unrolling the loop again.\n\nKeep three activities distinct:\n\n- **Verification** — `kprove` exits 0 and prints `#Top` under the supplied theory.\n- **Soundness audit** — proof extensions genuinely describe the program and do\n  not introduce inconsistent or execution-bypassing reasoning.\n- **Validation** — theorem scope, non-vacuity, trust, and independent evidence\n  support the intended property.\n\n## Choose the execution path first\n\nLive verification is the default. Use the on-paper fallback only when the user\nexplicitly requests it or the K toolchain cannot be made available.\n\nStart by checking the general K installer and version manager:\n\n```bash\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.nix-profile/bin:$PATH\"\ncommand -v kup\n```\n\nIf `kup` is available, stay on the live path. Install or repair the K package\nwith `kup install k` when necessary, then confirm the tools with\n`kompile --version && kprove --version`. See\n[installing-k.md](references/installing-k.md) for setup and\n[running-k.md](../shared/running-k.md) for shell and backend commands.\n\nIf `kup` is unavailable but an independently installed K toolchain already\nruns, stay on the live path. Otherwise offer installation first. Route to\n`reasoning-on-paper` only when installation is declined, impossible, or the\nuser asked for that mode.\n\n## Live workflow\n\n```text\nintent → code → semantics → spec → proof → #Top\n      → extension audit → adequacy → non-vacuity → evidence → exact-status report\n\nGate A PASS → continue to adequacy, non-vacuity, evidence, and status\nGate A FAIL → remove/disable offending extension → proving-spec → rebuild → #Top → Gate A\n```\n\nThe Gate A back-edge is internal iteration within the same agent invocation; it\nis not a retry, resume, second prompt, or fresh attempt. Preserve the current\nsolution and proof artifacts, remove the unsound extension, and continue the\noriginal one-shot workflow until Gate A passes or repair encounters an evidenced\nhard blocker. Every Gate A failure takes this back-edge unless an enumerated,\nevidenced hard blocker prevents further repair.\n\n| Stage | Artifact | Skill |\n|---|---|---|\n| Model the program's language | `semantics.k` | `writing-semantics` |\n| State the reachability property | `spec.k` | `writing-spec` |\n| Make the claims close | `verification.k` and `#Top` | `proving-spec` |\n| Check that the proof is honest and route Gate A failures back to construction | `PROOF.md` after status selection | `validating-proof` |\n\nUse `k-proof-technique` when the hard part is deriving an invariant, summary\nfunction, or proof obligation rather than running a pipeline stage.\n\n## On-paper fallback\n\nUse `reasoning-on-paper`. It produces `spec.k`, `verification.k`, and a\nnatural-language `REASONING.md` trace, all clearly marked `UNCHECKED`. It does\nnot create `semantics.k` and does not claim a machine-checked proof. On-paper\nwork inherits its proof-extension obligations through `k-proof-technique` while\nremaining `UNCHECKED`.\n\n## Shared references\n\n- [K syntax and operational semantics](../shared/k-syntax.md)\n- [K functions, claims, and proof modules](../shared/k-claims.md)\n- [Proof-extension soundness contract](../shared/proof-extension-soundness.md)\n- [Running the K tools](../shared/running-k.md)\n/codex-home/skills/k-proof-technique/SKILL.md:63:Read the [proof-extension soundness contract](../shared/proof-extension-soundness.md)\n/codex-home/skills/k-proof-technique/SKILL.md:97:If Gate A rejects an extension, remove or disable it and inspect the\n/codex-home/skills/k-proof-technique/SKILL.md:207:proof-extension contract before use:\n/codex-home/skills/k-proof-technique/SKILL.md:265:- [Proof-extension soundness contract](../shared/proof-extension-soundness.md) —\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:3:description: 'Use when kprove reports success (#Top) and you must audit proof-local functions, lemmas, or rewrites, theorem intent, or the trust boundary before writing PROOF.md.'\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:10:[proof-extension soundness contract](../shared/proof-extension-soundness.md) and\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:13:## Rebuild the proof-extension inventory\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:53:unwinds different computation is a Gate A failure.\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:82:   unconstrained—Gate A fails.\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:87:## Gate A — Real-program soundness\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:99:## Gate A failure: repair before reporting\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:101:Every Gate A failure takes this back-edge unless an enumerated, evidenced hard\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:103:not write `PROOF.md`. First remove or disable every offending extension,\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:106:construction, rebuild, recover `#Top`, and restart Gate A within the same agent\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:110:select terminal `Incomplete work`. Hard blockers are unavailable required tools\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:159:Gate B failure with Gate A passing yields `SOUND-BUT-LIMITED`.\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:186:universal equivalence, and they do not replace the Gate A obligation to connect\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:195:Gate A passes or repair attempts encounter an evidenced hard blocker. A hard\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:196:blocker leaves `Incomplete work`; after Gate A passes, Gate B failure is\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:200:## Write PROOF.md\n/codex-home/skills/validating-proof/SKILL.md:203:proof-extension inventory; exact commands and actual outputs; per-gate results;\n/codex-home/skills/writing-spec/SKILL.md:213:[proof-extension soundness contract](../shared/proof-extension-soundness.md),\n/codex-home/skills/writing-spec/SKILL.md:214:`validating-proof` applies the Gate A/B/C audit. Do not duplicate those checks\n/codex-home/skills/writing-spec/SKILL.md:228:- `validating-proof` — independently audits proof-extension soundness and\n/codex-home/skills/using-kit/SKILL.md:53:Gate A PASS → continue to adequacy, non-vacuity, evidence, and status\n/codex-home/skills/using-kit/SKILL.md:54:Gate A FAIL → remove/disable offending extension → proving-spec → rebuild → #Top → Gate A\n/codex-home/skills/using-kit/SKILL.md:57:The Gate A back-edge is internal iteration within the same agent invocation; it\n/codex-home/skills/using-kit/SKILL.md:60:original one-shot workflow until Gate A passes or repair encounters an evidenced\n/codex-home/skills/using-kit/SKILL.md:61:hard blocker. Every Gate A failure takes this back-edge unless an enumerated,\n/codex-home/skills/using-kit/SKILL.md:69:| Check that the proof is honest and route Gate A failures back to construction | `PROOF.md` after status selection | `validating-proof` |\n/codex-home/skills/using-kit/SKILL.md:79:work inherits its proof-extension obligations through `k-proof-technique` while\n/codex-home/skills/using-kit/SKILL.md:86:- [Proof-extension soundness contract](../shared/proof-extension-soundness.md)\n/codex-home/skills/proving-spec/SKILL.md:33:Read the [proof-extension soundness contract](../shared/proof-extension-soundness.md).\n/codex-home/skills/proving-spec/SKILL.md:81:## Same-session Gate A repair loop\n/codex-home/skills/proving-spec/SKILL.md:83:When `validating-proof` reports a Gate A failure, continue within the current\n/codex-home/skills/proving-spec/SKILL.md:103:7. Produce terminal `Incomplete work` only when repair attempts expose an\n/codex-home/skills/proving-spec/SKILL.md:107:restart Gate A. This loop is construction inside the original one-shot\n/codex-home/skills/proving-spec/SKILL.md:220:- [Proof-extension soundness contract](../shared/proof-extension-soundness.md) —\n/codex-home/skills/proving-spec/SKILL.md:231:  record, then applies Gate A — real-program soundness, Gate B — intent adequacy,\n/codex-home/skills/reasoning-on-paper/SKILL.md:21:Do not write `PROOF.md`, report `#Top`, or claim verification or validation.\n/codex-home/skills/shared/proof-extension-soundness.md:43:## Gate A — Real-program soundness\n/codex-home/skills/shared/proof-extension-soundness.md:45:Gate A is mandatory. A failed obligation means the proof does not establish the\n/codex-home/skills/shared/proof-extension-soundness.md:104:the proposed bridge and follow the Gate A repair transition. Finite tests can\n/codex-home/skills/shared/proof-extension-soundness.md:111:wrong branch, result, or observable state is a Gate A failure.\n/codex-home/skills/shared/proof-extension-soundness.md:164:## Gate A repair transition\n/codex-home/skills/shared/proof-extension-soundness.md:166:Gate A PASS continues to Gates B and C. Gate A failure is a repair signal, not\n/codex-home/skills/shared/proof-extension-soundness.md:167:a terminal result. Every Gate A failure takes this back-edge unless an\n/codex-home/skills/shared/proof-extension-soundness.md:174:   `#Top`, and reapply